1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Most of the Great Wall isn't brick.
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:06,500
Picture that famous stone wall near Beijing - it's the exception.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:11,500
For over 2,000 years, most of it was built from rammed earth.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:16,000
Earth packed between wooden boards, tamped down one layer at a time.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,500
In the desert, reeds and tamarisk went between the layers.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,500
Only the Ming faced it in brick - mostly the sections near Beijing.

7
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,500
Of 21,000 km surveyed, the brick wall is under 9,000.

8
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:30,500
Brick or earth - which lasts longer?
